      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Climate Considerations by Location"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "High-Elevation / Mountain Areas (Heber City, Park City, Sundance): High snow loads, intense UV radiation, and severe freeze-thaw cycles make standing seam metal or heavy-duty synthetic shakes the safest, lowest-maintenance bets. Avoid traditional clay or standard wood shakes which crack or rot under prolonged moisture and ice.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3,
              11
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Wasatch Front / Valleys (Salt Lake City, Provo, Ogden): Hot, dry summers combined with winter storms and occasional hail make Class 4 architectural shingles or metal the top picks for balancing cost, curb appeal, and weather resilience.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              12
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you share your city or elevation and whether your roof has a steep or low slope, I can give you a more specific material recommendation and cost estimate."
